The test `testSaslPlainServerBadPassword()` was failing because it was asserting an exact error message, which may not always match due to variations in the error output. This led to false negatives in the test results when the actual error message contained additional context or formatting differences. The modification to check for substrings instead of an exact match resolves this issue by allowing for more flexibility in the error message validation.

