assertEquals("PLAIN auth failed: wrong password", e.getMessage());
```
Reason:
The test was asserting an exact match of the error message returned by the `SaslException`. This strict comparison could lead to test failures if the actual error message contained additional context or formatting differences, resulting in false negatives.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
String message = e.getMessage();
assertContains("PLAIN auth failed", message);
assertContains("wrong password", message);
```
Reason:
The modification changes the assertion to check for substrings within the error message instead of requiring an exact match. This allows for variations in the error output while still validating that the essential components of the error message are present, thus preventing false negatives in the test results.


